/**
 * @name Smart Grid
 * @version 1.0.0
 * @author Jordan Steele
 * @destination script
 * @category Layer
 * @description Makes a smart grid from the selected layers in the current comp
 * @label GRID
 * @shift-click Adds null Grid Controller with parameters to control the grid
 * @cmd-click Removes the Grid Controller and bakes all the children to their current positions
 * @changelog New: New script to generate smart grid from selected layers
 */

/*  Smart Grid Layout for Selected Layers
    NORMAL run (no SHIFT):
      - Computes an “optimal” rows/cols grid for the selected layers
      - Fits all layers into cells with ONE global uniform scale (so everything fits)
      - Positions layers in the comp (no controller, no expressions, no parenting)

    SHIFT run:
      - Creates/uses a Null named "GRID_CONTROLLER" positioned at comp center
      - Applies controller pseudo effect (embedded .ffx binary bootstrap if missing)
      - Applies child pseudo effect to each selected layer
      - Parents selected layers to the controller (so moving controller moves the whole grid)
      - Writes baked content sizes/center into child effect
      - Adds expressions to Position + Scale
      - Child offsets are Offset X / Offset Y (sliders)
      - Controller Width/Height define the “grid box” size (defaults to comp size, overridable)
    
    COMMAND/CTRL run:
      - Bakes the selected GRID_CONTROLLER and its children to their current positions
      - Removes all expressions from children
      - Unparents children from controller
      - Removes GRID_CHILD effects
      - Deletes the GRID_CONTROLLER layer
*/

